.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions implement Phase 2 state operations for the bash\-server
v1 protocol.
Each function handles one protocol command, performs the requested
operation on the bash interpreter state, and writes a response back to
the client via \f[CR]protocol_write_line()\f[R].
.PP
All functions share the same signature:
\f[CR]int func(int wfd, const char *arg)\f[R].
.SH Variable Operations
\f[B]state_handle_get_var\f[R] \(em Looks up a variable with
\f[CR]find_variable()\f[R].
Returns \f[CR]VALUE <name> <base64> [attrs]\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]state_handle_set_var\f[R] \(em Parses
\f[CR]<name> <value> [\-\-export] [\-\-readonly] [\-\-integer]\f[R] from
\f[B]arg\f[R].
Calls \f[CR]bind_variable()\f[R] and optionally sets attribute flags.
Returns \f[CR]OK\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]state_handle_unset_var\f[R] \(em Checks if the variable is readonly
(returns \f[CR]ERR\f[R] if so), then calls \f[CR]unbind_variable()\f[R].
Returns \f[CR]OK\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.SH Function Operations
\f[B]state_handle_get_func\f[R] \(em Looks up a function with
\f[CR]find_function()\f[R].
Serializes the definition with \f[CR]named_function_string()\f[R] and
returns \f[CR]FUNC <name> <base64>\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]state_handle_unset_func\f[R] \(em Verifies function exists, then
calls \f[CR]parse_and_execute(\(dqunset \-f <name>\(dq)\f[R] to remove
it.
Returns \f[CR]OK\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.SH Alias Operations
\f[B]state_handle_get_alias\f[R] \(em Looks up alias value with
\f[CR]get_alias_value()\f[R].
Returns \f[CR]ALIAS <name> <base64>\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]state_handle_set_alias\f[R] \(em Parses \f[CR]<name> <value>\f[R]
from \f[B]arg\f[R].
Calls \f[CR]add_alias()\f[R].
Returns \f[CR]OK\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]state_handle_unset_alias\f[R] \(em Calls \f[CR]remove_alias()\f[R].
Returns \f[CR]OK\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR alias not found\f[R].
.SH Trap Operations
\f[B]state_handle_set_trap\f[R] \(em Parses
\f[CR]<signal> <command>\f[R] from \f[B]arg\f[R].
Decodes signal name with \f[CR]decode_signal()\f[R], then calls
\f[CR]set_signal()\f[R].
Returns \f[CR]OK\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]state_handle_unset_trap\f[R] \(em Decodes signal name, calls
\f[CR]restore_default_signal()\f[R].
Returns \f[CR]OK\f[R] or \f[CR]ERR\f[R].
.SH Inspection
\f[B]state_handle_inspect\f[R] \(em Parses \f[CR]<target> [pattern]\f[R]
from \f[B]arg\f[R].
Enumerates shell state and sends multiple response lines followed by
\f[CR]INSPECT\-END\f[R].
.PP
