.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
All state operations use the v1 line\-oriented protocol.
The v2 JSON session handler dispatches state operations on
\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R] (channel 2) but the underlying functions still use
\f[CR]protocol_write_line()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Variable values are base64\-encoded to safely transmit binary data and
special characters over the line\-oriented protocol.
.IP \(bu 2
SET\-VAR parses flags (\f[CR]\-\-export\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-readonly\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-integer\f[R]) that may appear after the value.
The value itself extends from after the name to the first flag or end of
string.
.IP \(bu 2
UNSET\-VAR checks for readonly before unsetting and returns an error
rather than allowing bash to print its own error message.
.IP \(bu 2
UNSET\-FUNC uses \f[CR]parse_and_execute(\(dqunset \-f name\(dq)\f[R]
because there is no direct C API equivalent to the \f[CR]unset \-f\f[R]
builtin.
.IP \(bu 2
Signal names for traps are decoded case\-insensitively via
\f[CR]decode_signal()\f[R] with \f[CR]DSIG_NOCASE\f[R].
